  "description": "Where a file path with a line is a reference in the text of a reply or of terminal output, the rule of the Mac's FilePathLinks and of the desktop client's file_links. A reference is a relative path, at least one directory or a dot in the name, then :line and optionally :column, both counted from 1 in the text; the expected line and column count from 0. A path that is absolute or has an empty, dot or dot-dot component is not one. The label is the text the reference takes, with its dot-slash. Both clients pass every case.",
